      "file": "flare_knockout_drum_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Slow the gas so liquid drops out",
      "description": "Relief streams often carry liquid; a burning liquid rain from the flare is dangerous. The KO drum is sized (API 521 method) so the vapour velocity is low enough for droplets of ≈ 300–600 µm to settle in the travel time between inlet and outlet, and with hold-up volume for the liquid from the largest relief case for ≈ 20–30 min. It operates near atmospheric pressure, so pressure drop is kept small; pump-out pumps empty it.",
